      "hints": [
        "Locate midpoint $P$ of $OD$ and midpoint $Q$ of $GF$.",
        "Use $\\overrightarrow{PB}=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OP}$ and $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\overrightarrow{OQ}-\\overrightarrow{OP}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac12(2,0,10)=(1,0,5)$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=(6,8,0)$, and $\\overrightarrow{OQ}=(5,8,10)$.",
        "$\\overrightarrow{PB}=(6,8,0)-(1,0,5)=(5,8,-5)$; $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=(5,8,10)-(1,0,5)=(4,8,5)$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_w19_12_q7_ii",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m01_l03"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Compare the squared lengths of $\\overrightarrow{PB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$.",
        "The smaller squared distance identifies the nearer point."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$|PB|^2=5^2+8^2+(-5)^2=114$; $|PQ|^2=4^2+8^2+5^2=105$.",
        "Since $105<114$, $P$ is nearer to $Q$ than to $B$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_w19_12_q7_iii",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m02_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Angle $BPQ$ is between the two vectors from $P$ in (i).",
        "Use their dot product and lengths."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{PB}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{PQ}=5(4)+8(8)+(-5)(5)=59$.",
        "$|PB|=\\sqrt{114}$ and $|PQ|=\\sqrt{105}$, hence $\\angle BPQ=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{59}{\\sqrt{114}\\sqrt{105}}\\right)=57.4^\\circ$ (3 s.f.)."
      ]
    }
  ]
